![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Using `new RegExp('^' + entry + '$', 'm')` to match lines in `.env.example` can fail on platforms or checkouts that use CRLF (\r\n) line endings because the `$` anchor in JavaScript's multiline RegExp matches before \n but includes the \r carriage return. Additionally, constructing a RegExp directly from strings containing dots (like `oss-cn-hongkong.aliyuncs.com`) treats them as regex wildcards rather than literal dots.

To make the test robust across different platforms and avoid regex escaping issues, normalize CRLF line endings to LF or split the file content by lines and perform an exact match check.

```suggestion
  const backendLines = backendEnv.split(/\r?\n/);
  for (const entry of required) {
    assert.ok(backendLines.includes(entry), 'Missing expected env entry: ' + entry);
  }
```

